+Joy Image Edit opts into this epilogue only at `quality="high"` on SM120,
+including RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell. Its BF16 image MLP uses the fused path for
+batch 1 with 8192 image tokens and a 4096-to-16384 projection, as in the
+1024 x 1024 single-reference editing workload. The smaller text MLP retains
+its separate projection and activation. The epilogue changes BF16 rounding;
+`exact` and `lossless` retain the original image MLP. Quantized projections,
+active dynamic LoRA, other shapes or devices, and `torch.compile` also use
+the original path. This does not add model-level BCG support.
